k=10 UNION-BOUND ROUTE (kps-S75): does an unconditional mu-floor close the wide residual?
================================================================================
min meas(G_P) |P|=3 = 55/91 = 0.6044 at P=(1,12,13)  =>  union needs mu(E) >= 0.4521
mu_{1/7}(AP_10) = 38/49 = 0.7755  (unconditional; the CONDITIONAL rho* = 0.398)

UNCONDITIONAL mu of wide structured families (true, numeric):
  [0,2,4,6,8,9,10,11,12,48] diam48: true mu = 1.0000   D_q-window(q<=6) floor = 0.0888
  [0,2,4,6,8,10,12,14,16,17] diam17: true mu = 0.8338   D_q-window floor = 0.2615
  dilated-AP_10 + primitivity perturbation (d=3..11): true mu = 0.826-0.834
  => true mu is HIGH (0.77-1.0) but the D_q-window (q<=6) floor captures only 0.05-0.26.

VERDICT: the union bound needs mu >= 0.4521; the proven elementary floors give:
  tent (unconditional)         mu >= 8/35 = 0.229    (short)
  D_q-window (q<=6, no teeth)   mu >= 0.05-0.26       (short)
Neither reaches 0.4521.  The gap 0.229 -> 0.4521 for structured wide families IS a
density-floor statement (the higher-q ladder + bulk carry the rest of mu).  So k=10's
structured-wide residual = the R2/density-floor rigidity, with a comfortable margin
(need 0.45, truth 0.77).  Natural engine: klein-S175 second-moment spread floor (HYP-4991).
